{"crc":"a41413ee","kind":"Candidate","payload":{"response":"Looking at the issue, a `socket.error` is being raised from `urllib3/response.py` during `read()` operations but isn't being caught and wrapped in a requests exception. The error propagates up through the call stack without being converted to a `ConnectionError`.\n\nThe fix should catch `socket.error` in the `read()` method of `HTTPResponse` in `urllib3/response.py` and raise a `ProtocolError` (which will then be caught by requests and converted to a `ConnectionError`).\n\nHere's the edit:\n\n# path: requests/packages/urllib3/response.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n            except SocketTimeout:\n                # FIXME: Ideally we'd like to include the url in the ReadTimeoutError but\n                # there is yet no clean way to get at it from this context.\n                raise ReadTimeoutError(self._pool, None, 'Read timed out.')\n\n            except BaseSSLError as e:\n                # FIXME: Is there a better way to differentiate between SSLErrors?\n                if not 'read operation timed out' in str(e):  # Defensive:\n                    # This shouldn't happen but just in case we're missing an edge\n                    # case, let's avoid swallowing SSL errors.\n                    raise\n\n                raise ReadTimeoutError(self._pool, None, 'Read timed out.')\n\n            except HTTPException as e:\n                # This includes IncompleteRead.\n                raise ProtocolError('Connection broken: %r' % e, e)\n=======\n            except SocketTimeout:\n                # FIXME: Ideally we'd like to include the url in the ReadTimeoutError but\n                # there is yet no clean way to get at it from this context.\n                raise ReadTimeoutError(self._pool, None, 'Read timed out.')\n\n            except BaseSSLError as e:\n                # FIXME: Is there a better way to differentiate between SSLErrors?\n                if not 'read operation timed out' in str(e):  # Defensive:\n                    # This shouldn't happen but just in case we're missing an edge\n                    # case, let's avoid swallowing SSL errors.\n                    raise\n\n                raise ReadTimeoutError(self._pool, None, 'Read timed out.')\n\n            except HTTPException as e:\n                # This includes IncompleteRead.\n                raise ProtocolError('Connection broken: %r' % e, e)\n\n            except socket.error as e:\n                raise ProtocolError('Connection broken: %r' % e, e)\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":0},"producer":{"instance":"01KZT14B240VJ5SBVACGV07QRY","kind":"drafter","parent":"01KZT14B20ME10YBNMQK9H5P3Q"},"schema":"Candidate@1","seq":14,"t":1786506265.473152}
{"crc":"53d33754","kind":"substrate.TriggerFired","payload":{"factory":"validator","firing_key":null,"input_sha256":"sha256:90461314485acdbe721ff71c08ccc6b8f6ded39e6ec40ffc26810f2b4f861f75","instance":"01KZT14GW1WQ8HVB6VD4ECQAWV","resolved_input":{"response":"Looking at the issue, a `socket.error` is being raised from `urllib3/response.py` during `read()` operations but isn't being caught and wrapped in a requests exception. The error propagates up through the call stack without being converted to a `ConnectionError`.\n\nThe fix should catch `socket.error` in the `read()` method of `HTTPResponse` in `urllib3/response.py` and raise a `ProtocolError` (which will then be caught by requests and converted to a `ConnectionError`).\n\nHere's the edit:\n\n# path: requests/packages/urllib3/response.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n            except SocketTimeout:\n                # FIXME: Ideally we'd like to include the url in the ReadTimeoutError but\n                # there is yet no clean way to get at it from this context.\n                raise ReadTimeoutError(self._pool, None, 'Read timed out.')\n\n            except BaseSSLError as e:\n                # FIXME: Is there a better way to differentiate between SSLErrors?\n                if not 'read operation timed out' in str(e):  # Defensive:\n                    # This shouldn't happen but just in case we're missing an edge\n                    # case, let's avoid swallowing SSL errors.\n                    raise\n\n                raise ReadTimeoutError(self._pool, None, 'Read timed out.')\n\n            except HTTPException as e:\n                # This includes IncompleteRead.\n                raise ProtocolError('Connection broken: %r' % e, e)\n=======\n            except SocketTimeout:\n                # FIXME: Ideally we'd like to include the url in the ReadTimeoutError but\n                # there is yet no clean way to get at it from this context.\n                raise ReadTimeoutError(self._pool, None, 'Read timed out.')\n\n            except BaseSSLError as e:\n                # FIXME: Is there a better way to differentiate between SSLErrors?\n                if not 'read operation timed out' in str(e):  # Defensive:\n                    # This shouldn't happen but just in case we're missing an edge\n                    # case, let's avoid swallowing SSL errors.\n                    raise\n\n                raise ReadTimeoutError(self._pool, None, 'Read timed out.')\n\n            except HTTPException as e:\n                # This includes IncompleteRead.\n                raise ProtocolError('Connection broken: %r' % e, e)\n\n            except socket.error as e:\n                raise ProtocolError('Connection broken: %r' % e, e)\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":0},"trigger_id":"validate"},"producer":null,"schema":"substrate.TriggerFired@1","seq":15,"t":1786506265.473419}
